{"api_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/37670","collected_at":"2026-09-27T21:56:42.768501+00:00","comments":[{"author_association":"COLLABORATOR","body":"I think this is expected: in general JAX (via XLA) uses flush-to-zero semantics for subnormals; see https://docs.jax.dev/en/latest/notebooks/Common_Gotchas_in_JAX.html#miscellaneous-divergences-from-numpy for a mention of this.\n\nBecause `log(0)` is `-inf`, the outputs you're seeing above are what we would expect.\n\n> A documentation clarification — or ideally a runtime warning when a log-family function receives an input flushed to zero — would prevent silent failures.\n\nIt's documented in sharp bits; I think it would be overkill to re-document this behavior in every function's doc string.\n\nRegarding a runtime warning, that's difficult to do without severe performance penalties. For operations on accelerators, there is no efficient mechanism to propagate warnings back to the host that are conditional on values that appear within arrays at runtime.","created_at":"2026-05-16T01:56:44Z","html_url":"https://github.com/jax-ml/jax/issues/37670#issuecomment-4465076682","id":4465076682,"issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/37670","minimized":null,"node_id":"IC_kwDOCTkjjc8AAAABCiOpyg","performed_via_github_app":null,"pin":null,"reactions":{"+1":0,"-1":0,"confused":0,"eyes":0,"heart":0,"hooray":0,"laugh":0,"rocket":0,"total_count":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/4465076682/reactions"},"updated_at":"2026-05-16T02:01:48Z","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jax-ml/jax/issues/comments/4465076682","user":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/781659?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jakevdp/gists{/gist_id}","grava